# The ignore file BuildKit actually uses for this Dockerfile: a `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` next to it
# takes precedence over the repository root's `.dockerignore`, and every build here is
# `-f solution/engine/Dockerfile`, so this is the one that decides (LEASH-141).
#
# The image must be built from the repository, not from whatever the developer happens to have
# installed or left lying about: `COPY solution/app/ ./` runs after `npm ci`, so a host `node_modules`
# would overwrite the layer the lockfile produced, and the artifact APP_REVISION labels would not be the
# one the lockfile describes.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
solution/app/dist
solution/app/test-results
solution/app/playwright-report
solution/kanban
solution/docs
solution/prototype
solution/training/data
.git
# Secrets never belong in a build context: anything copied in is readable in the image's layers.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
